## Embedded Fonts

### CaptchAPI Glyphs Bold (SIL OFL 1.1)

`assets/fonts/CaptchAPIGlyphs-Bold.ttf` is compiled into the CaptchAPI binary
via `include_bytes!` and used to render CAPTCHA glyphs.

It is a **Modified Version** under the SIL Open Font License: Liberation Sans
Bold 2.1.5, subset to the 54 characters CaptchAPI actually renders (7,360
bytes, down from 414,568). It is regenerated by `scripts/subset-font.py`.

- Derived from: Liberation Sans Bold 2.1.5
- Upstream: https://github.com/liberationfonts
- License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2010 Google Corporation with Reserved Font Name
  Arimo, Tinos and Cousine; Copyright (c) 2012 Red Hat, Inc. with Reserved
  Font Name Liberation.

OFL compliance notes:

- The subset is renamed to "CaptchAPI Glyphs" so that no Reserved Font Name
  appears in any of its naming records (name IDs 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 16, 17), as
  clause 3 requires of Modified Versions. Provenance is recorded in the
  description record (name ID 10), which the OFL FAQ permits.
- The original copyright (name ID 0), license (13) and license URL (14)
  records are preserved verbatim in the face.
- The font remains under the OFL and is not sold separately.
- CaptchAPI is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Liberation Fonts
  project or its copyright holders.

The full license text is distributed alongside the font at
`assets/fonts/LICENSE-Liberation-OFL-1.1.txt`.

Liberation Sans is metric-compatible with Arial. It replaces the Monotype
Arial that `captcha-rs` v0.5.0 embeds; that font is proprietary and its
embedded license notice forbids redistribution, so it could not be shipped
in CaptchAPI's binaries or container images.

